# MC-X-F11: an answer never depends on the order of its terms (L §5.11; E §3.1 step 5, §3.2). total[2027] reads the
# legs of contribs, whose refusal rests on the walk up to their day (E §4.2 step 5); refund[y], dated by a window after
# y, reads back[y], which reads the fill over total[y]. A walk up to a day books nothing after it, and a movement dated
# by a window falls after that day when the window's first day does (L §4.4), so refund[2027] (window(2028-01-01,
# 2028-02-01)) isn't evaluated for the legs of 2027. snap11 refused t (RUN-CYCLE total[2027] reads itself through a
# computed key) and printed t2. The supply total[y] equals the sum of the demands, so every demand is taken whole
# (L §5.12 Take) and both differences are 0.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind contribs: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place acct: claims PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2025-01-01..
def total[y in years]: money PLN = sum(c.cash.amount for c in contribs over y)
fill f[y in years]
  supply total[y]
  demand c.cash.amount for c in contribs over y
  arc true
  order c.day
def back[y in years]: money PLN = sum(f[y].taken[c] for c in contribs over y)
move pay[m in months]: contribs
  on start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to acct amount minor(PLN)
move refund[y in years]: transfers
  on window(end_of(y), add_months(end_of(y), 1))
  leg cash from acct to world amount back[y]
ask t: total[2027] - back[2027]
ask t2: back[2027] - total[2027]
=== expect
t: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
t2: 0.00 PLN
  cut 2025-01-01
